# L §4.2 (round 13b): "the last day of a period is end_of(p) - 1 day, since end_of is the first day after it";
# start_of/end_of "the first day of period k; the first day after it"; overlap_days(a, b, k) counts the days of k in
# [a, b]: 2026-02-20 .. 2026-03-31 holds 9 days of February 2026 (20th to 28th); last_business(p, 1, cal) is p's last
# business day, 2026-02-27 a Friday (2026-02-28 a Saturday, weekends [sat, sun]).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input len: calendar

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2025-12-01
  len = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])

ask q: end_of(2026-02), end_of(2026-02) - 1 day, overlap_days(2026-02-20, 2026-03-31, 2026-02)
ask r: last_business(2026-02, 1, len)
=== expect
q: (2026-03-01, 2026-02-28, 9)
  cut 2026-12-31
r: 2026-02-27
  cut 2026-12-31
